reims-vgpu: every XR fragment output reaches its encoder as binary16.

Metal: the AGX pixel write of an XR (PBE15) attachment is a Half4 partition
transfer: the value the hardware encoder quantizes, with
round-to-nearest-even, is the fragment output rounded to binary16, for
blended, replacement and unblended writes alike.
Before: only the shader-evaluated blend path rounded to binary16 (its clamped
source and every blend step). An unblended or replacement XR write quantized
the shader's Float32 value, so a colour such as 0.51875 stored code 649 from
one draw and 648 (its binary16 value 0.518555) from a source-over draw of the
same colour.
Now: `color_quantization::rewrite` declares `OutputPrecision::Binary16` for
every XR output; the translator rounds each channel once before the RTNE
encoder. The three writes store one code. A clear keeps its Float32
quantization: no partition is recovered for it.
Test: `vk_engine_parity::an_xr_fragment_output_reaches_its_encoder_as_binary16`
on RADV: 0.51875 stores 648 (649 before) on 554, 550 and as the XR alpha of
553; 0.75 and -0.25 are exact ties (766.5, 256.5) that store 766 and 256 for
all three blend states.

